---
export const prerender = true;
import '../../../styles/global.css';
import '../../../styles/cai-doc.css';
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow" />
  <title>Cultivated AI · Mission Control · Pre-workshop interview · The Baker's Dozen</title>
  <style>
    .cd-q-type { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.58rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--bar, var(--doc-accent)); margin-left: 0.5rem; vertical-align: 0.1em; opacity: 0.8; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="cd-shell" style="--doc-accent: var(--color-sky);">

    <div class="cd-printhint screen-only">
      <span class="accent">Send or print →</span>
      Two versions help: one for each leader, one for whoever owns the data. About twenty minutes.
    </div>

    <p class="cd-eyebrow">Cultivated AI · Mission Control · before we begin</p>
    <h1 class="cd-title">Show us your <em>data world</em>.</h1>
    <p class="cd-lede">Mission Control is a build. The more we know about your sources, your real questions, and your access before Session 1, the more we get built in the room instead of scoped in the room. <strong>Honest answers beat tidy ones.</strong></p>
    <p class="cd-meta">18 questions · ~20 min · leadership + data owners · The Baker's Dozen</p>
    <div class="cd-rule"></div>

    <!-- 01 -->
    <section class="cd-section" style="--bar: var(--color-sky);">
      <div class="cd-section-rule"></div>
      <div class="cd-section-head"><span class="cd-section-num">Part 01</span><h2 class="cd-section-name">You and your <em>numbers</em></h2></div>
      <ol class="cd-qlist">
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q01</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">What's your role, and which decisions should your data be informing?</p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">We aim Mission Control at the decisions you actually own.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q02</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">When you need a number today, how do you get it? <span class="cd-q-type">Open Power BI / ask an analyst / wait for a report</span></p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">This tells us how far you are from "just ask."</p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q03</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">How long does a typical "can someone pull me X" usually take to come back?</p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">The lag is the cost we're removing.</p>
        </div></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- 02 -->
    <section class="cd-section" style="--bar: var(--color-purple);">
      <div class="cd-section-rule"></div>
      <div class="cd-section-head"><span class="cd-section-num">Part 02</span><h2 class="cd-section-name">Your data sources <em>today</em></h2></div>
      <p class="cd-section-blurb">This is the raw material of Session 1's inventory. The more concrete, the better.</p>
      <ol class="cd-qlist">
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q04</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">What lives in Power BI today, and who maintains it?</p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">Your existing semantic models are the fastest on-ramp, if they're clean.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q05</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">What does GobbleCube give you (city, store, platform), and how do you access it?</p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">We need to know how that data gets out and on what cadence.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q06</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">Where do production and supply-chain numbers live, and is either connected to anything else?</p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">These are the sources you mentioned wanting to plug in. We'll plan for them.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q07</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">Does all of this come together anywhere already, even partially? <span class="cd-q-type">A warehouse / a master sheet / nothing yet</span></p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">Tells us whether we're choosing a warehouse or improving one.</p>
        </div></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- 03 -->
    <section class="cd-section" style="--bar: var(--color-teal);">
      <div class="cd-section-rule"></div>
      <div class="cd-section-head"><span class="cd-section-num">Part 03</span><h2 class="cd-section-name">The questions you wish you could <em>just ask</em></h2></div>
      <ol class="cd-qlist">
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q08</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">Name five questions you'd ask your data every week if the answer were instant.</p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">These become the golden questions that anchor the whole build.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q09</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">Which questions do you <em>not</em> bother asking today because it's too slow to find out?</p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">The unasked questions are often where the impact hides.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q10</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">When two reports disagree, which one wins, and why?</p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">This surfaces the metric-definition conflicts the semantic layer has to settle.</p>
        </div></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- 04 -->
    <section class="cd-section" style="--bar: var(--color-amber);">
      <div class="cd-section-rule"></div>
      <div class="cd-section-head"><span class="cd-section-num">Part 04</span><h2 class="cd-section-name">High-impact problems and the <em>AI lens</em></h2></div>
      <ol class="cd-qlist">
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q11</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">Name one high-impact problem where faster, better data would change the decision. <span class="cd-q-type">Wastage / fill rate / promo ROI / ...</span></p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">We work one of these end to end in Session 3, live.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q12</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">For that problem, what does "good" look like in 90 days?</p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">We point the roadmap at a result you'd recognise, not a demo.</p>
        </div></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- 05 -->
    <section class="cd-section" style="--bar: var(--color-navy);">
      <div class="cd-section-rule"></div>
      <div class="cd-section-head"><span class="cd-section-num">Part 05</span><h2 class="cd-section-name">Governance and <em>access</em></h2></div>
      <ol class="cd-qlist">
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q13</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">Who should and should not see what, across cities, teams, and finance? Any sensitive data?</p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">We inherit access rules from the warehouse, but you decide them.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q14</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">What would have to be true for you to act on an answer from an AI, not just a human analyst?</p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">That answer defines the trust surface we build in Session 2.</p>
        </div></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- 06 -->
    <section class="cd-section" style="--bar: var(--color-accent-red);">
      <div class="cd-section-rule"></div>
      <div class="cd-section-head"><span class="cd-section-num">Part 06</span><h2 class="cd-section-name">Showing up in <em>AI answers</em></h2></div>
      <ol class="cd-qlist">
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q15</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">Ask ChatGPT or Gemini "best [your category] in India" right now. Does Baker's Dozen show up?</p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">Do it before the workshop. Whatever you find is the starting line for Session 4.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q16</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">Where do your shoppers actually discover and vet products? <span class="cd-q-type">Reddit / YouTube / marketplaces / word of mouth</span></p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">These are the sources AI answers lean on, so they're where we'll focus.</p>
        </div></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- 07 -->
    <section class="cd-section" style="--bar: var(--color-sky);">
      <div class="cd-section-rule"></div>
      <div class="cd-section-head"><span class="cd-section-num">Part 07</span><h2 class="cd-section-name">Readiness</h2></div>
      <ol class="cd-qlist">
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q17</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">Who from the data side will be in the room, and can they arrange read access to the sources before Session 1?</p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">Access sorted in advance is the single biggest thing that keeps Session 1 moving.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q18</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">Anything else we should know to make these sessions productive?</p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">Constraints, politics, past attempts. All useful.</p>
        </div></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <div class="cd-callout" style="--bar: var(--color-sky); margin-top: 2.75rem;">
      <h4>Before Session 1</h4>
      <p>Send your answers, and make sure the data owners can get us <em>read access</em> to Power BI, GobbleCube exports, and the production / supply-chain files. See the pre-requisites list.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cd-footer">
      <span class="brand">Cultivated AI · <em>Grow, don't Chase.</em></span>
      <span>Mission Control · pre-workshop interview</span>
    </div>

  </div>
</body>
</html>
